#Day 5: Instruction Hierarchy & Prompt Injection

#What I Learned

- AI systems can receive instructions from different sources.
- System, developer, and user instructions can have different priorities.
- Prompt injection attempts to influence model behavior through crafted input.
- Indirect prompt injection can come from external content such as webpages or documents.
- Authentication and authorization should be handled by the application, not trusted to the LLM.

## Key Takeaway

> The model should not be treated as the security boundary.

## Red Teaming Connection

Testing conflicting instructions helps evaluate how reliably an AI system follows its intended behavior.
